================================================================================
                   GDB CHEAT SHEET — STM32 / FreeRTOS
================================================================================

1. START GDB & CONNECT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terminal 1: Start OpenOCD
openocd -f interface/cmsis-dap.cfg -f target/stm32h7x.cfg

# Terminal 2: Start GDB with TUI
gdb-multiarch -tui build/firmware.elf

# Inside GDB
target extended-remote localhost:3333   Connect to OpenOCD
monitor reset halt                       Reset and halt MCU
monitor reset run                        Reset and run MCU
load                                     Flash ELF to MCU
file firmware.elf                        Load executable and symbols
quit / q                                 Exit GDB


2. EXECUTION CONTROL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
continue / c          Resume execution
step / s              Step INTO function
next / n              Step OVER function
finish / fin          Step OUT of function
stepi / si            Execute one assembly instruction
nexti / ni            Step over one assembly instruction
until / u             Continue until a later location (often exits a loop)
return 0              Force current function to return 0
Ctrl-C                Interrupt running program

REMEMBER:
    step    -> INTO
    next    -> OVER
    finish  -> OUT


3. BREAKPOINTS & WATCHPOINTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
break main                  Break at function
b main.c:42                 Break at source line
break *0x08000100           Break at address
tbreak main                 Temporary breakpoint
hbreak main                 Hardware breakpoint

break main.c:42 if x == 10  Conditional breakpoint
condition 1 x > 100         Add/change condition on breakpoint 1

watch x                     Stop when x changes
rwatch x                    Stop when x is read
awatch x                    Stop when x is accessed

info breakpoints            List breakpoints/watchpoints
delete 1                    Delete breakpoint 1
delete                      Delete all breakpoints
disable 1                   Disable breakpoint 1
enable 1                    Enable breakpoint 1
clear main                  Remove breakpoint at main
ignore 1 10                 Ignore next 10 hits of breakpoint 1


4. INSPECT VARIABLES & EXPRESSIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
p x                         Print variable
p/x x                       Print hexadecimal
p/d x                       Print decimal
p/t x                       Print binary
p/c x                       Print character

p *ptr                      Dereference pointer
p &x                        Print address of variable
p array[3]                  Inspect array element
p obj.member                Inspect struct member
p ptr->member               Inspect member through pointer

p x == 0                    Evaluate comparison
p x == pdFALSE              Compare against macro (requires macro info)
p (int)state                Print enum as integer
p sizeof(x)                 Print size of variable

display x                   Auto-print x whenever execution stops
info display                List auto-display expressions
undisplay 1                 Remove display 1

info locals                 Show local variables
info args                   Show function arguments
ptype x                     Show detailed type
whatis x                    Show variable type

set var x = 10              Modify variable value
set print pretty on         Pretty-print structs

# Macros (compile with -g3)
info macro pdFALSE          Show macro definition
macro expand pdFALSE        Expand macro


5. MEMORY & REGISTERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
info registers              Show CPU registers
p $pc                       Program counter
p $sp                       Stack pointer
p $lr                       Link register
p $xpsr                     Program status register (Cortex-M)

x/4wx 0x20000000            Read 4 words in hexadecimal
x/16bx 0x20000000           Read 16 bytes in hexadecimal
x/10i $pc                   Show 10 instructions at PC
x/s ptr                     Examine null-terminated string

MEMORY SYNTAX:
    x/NFU ADDRESS

    N = Number of units
    F = Format:
        x = hexadecimal
        d = decimal
        t = binary
        i = instruction
        s = string
    U = Unit size:
        b = 1 byte
        h = 2 bytes
        w = 4 bytes
        g = 8 bytes

disassemble main            Disassemble function
disassemble /s main         Source + assembly (if source info available)
disassemble /r main         Include instruction bytes


6. SOURCE CODE NAVIGATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
list / l                    Show source code
list main                   Show source around function
list main.c:42              Show source near line 42
list tasks.c:100            Show code in another file
list *$pc                   Show source near current PC

set listsize 30             Show 30 lines per list
info sources                List source files
info functions              List functions
info variables              List global/static variables
info line main              Show function source location
directory /path/to/src      Add source search path
set substitute-path OLD NEW Remap source paths

NOTE: 'list' only displays code. It does not change execution.
WARNING: 'jump' changes the program counter and execution flow!


7. CALL STACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
backtrace / bt              Show call stack
bt full                     Show stack + local variables
frame 0                     Select current frame
frame 1                     Select caller frame
up                          Move to caller frame
down                        Move to callee frame
info frame                  Inspect selected frame

NOTE: 'up' and 'down' navigate stack frames without executing code.


8. FREERTOS DEBUGGING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
p pxCurrentTCB              Current task's TCB pointer
p pxCurrentTCB->pcTaskName  Current task name
p pxCurrentTCB->uxPriority  Current task priority

break vMyTask               Stop when task function is reached
break vTaskDelay            Stop when task calls vTaskDelay
break vTaskSwitchContext    Stop during task context selection

info threads                List tasks (requires RTOS-aware OpenOCD)
thread 2                    Select task 2 (if supported)
thread apply all bt         Show stack trace for all recognized tasks

NOTE:
- pxCurrentTCB is a FreeRTOS internal variable.
- A task may be Running, Ready, Blocked, or Suspended.
- 'info threads' requires suitable RTOS-awareness support.
- Breakpoints affect real-time behavior.


9. GDB TUI
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gdb-multiarch -tui firmware.elf    Start GDB TUI

tui enable                  Enable TUI
tui disable                 Disable TUI

layout src                  Show source
layout asm                  Show assembly
layout split                Show source + assembly
layout regs                 Show registers alongside source/assembly
layout next                 Cycle layouts

tui reg general             Display general registers
focus src                   Focus source window
focus cmd                   Focus command window
refresh                     Refresh screen

Ctrl-x a                    Toggle TUI
Ctrl-x 2                    Cycle layouts
Ctrl-l                      Refresh screen

NOTE:
When source window is focused, arrow keys scroll source code.


10. USEFUL EXTRAS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
help COMMAND                Show command documentation
apropos keyword             Search commands by keyword
show version                Show GDB version
set pagination off          Disable pagination
set print pretty on         Pretty-print structures
set print elements 0        Remove array element printing limit
set confirm off             Disable confirmation prompts
source commands.gdb         Execute GDB script


11. COMMON DEBUGGING WORKFLOW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Start GDB
gdb-multiarch -tui build/firmware.elf

# Connect to MCU
(gdb) target extended-remote localhost:3333

# Reset and halt
(gdb) monitor reset halt

# Set breakpoint
(gdb) break main

# Run until breakpoint
(gdb) continue

# Inspect current state
(gdb) info locals
(gdb) info registers
(gdb) bt

# Step through code
(gdb) next
(gdb) step
(gdb) finish

# Inspect variables
(gdb) p xReturn
(gdb) p xReturn == 0
(gdb) p/x xReturn

# Inspect task
(gdb) p pxCurrentTCB->pcTaskName

# Watch variable
(gdb) watch counter

# Continue execution
(gdb) continue


